---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MarketResearchForm from '../components/MarketResearchForm.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DAJC Platform | European Heavy & Oversized Transport Coordination"
  description="Discover the planned DAJC Platform: provider-neutral coordination for heavy and oversized transport, connecting transport context, routes, permits, documents and execution. Share your industry feedback."
>
  <main class="product-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">DAJC PLATFORM · HEAVY & OVERSIZED TRANSPORT</p>
      <h1>One transport.<br /><em>One coordinated process.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">Complex transport involves more than moving a load. DAJC Platform is being designed as a provider-neutral coordination layer that connects the people, documents, permits and operational steps around one transport — while respecting the systems companies already use.</p>
      <p class="status">In development · Pre-production testing planned for Q3 2027. Features and third-party integrations described here are proposed, not live production capabilities.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#research">Share your industry feedback</a>
        <a class="outline" href="https://demo.dajc.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore illustrative demo ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p class="small">The demo uses synthetic data and is not evidence of live permits, routing feeds or customer integrations.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="audience-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">WHO IT IS FOR</p>
      <h2 id="audience-title">For the professionals who plan, arrange and execute complex transport.</h2>
      <div class="grid audience">
        <article><h3>Heavy & oversized carriers</h3><p>Coordinate orders, equipment, permits and execution across your operational team.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Dispatchers & drivers</h3><p>Work with the relevant approved route, instructions, updates and evidence in context.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Shippers & logistics teams</h3><p>Follow agreed milestones and handovers without managing separate information chains.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Specialist partners</h3><p>Support authorised permit, escort and route-related workflows with clear responsibilities.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="problem-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE PROBLEM</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title">The information exists. The complete picture often does not.</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article><span class="num">01</span><h3>Fragmented communication</h3><p>Transport instructions arrive by email, phone and separate customer or dispatch systems.</p></article>
        <article><span class="num">02</span><h3>Routes, permits, restrictions</h3><p>Changing conditions require checks across several specialists, sources and authorities.</p></article>
        <article><span class="num">03</span><h3>Scattered documentation</h3><p>Supporting files and approvals can be difficult to find at the moment they are needed.</p></article>
        <article><span class="num">04</span><h3>Repeated work and unclear handovers</h3><p>The same changes may be entered or confirmed repeatedly, leaving gaps in accountability.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="solution-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE PROPOSED SOLUTION</p>
      <h2 id="solution-title">One D-ID transport context, connected to the workflow.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">DAJC is not intended to replace your TMS, navigation, permit specialist or existing service providers. It aims to connect the relevant information and actions so authorised participants can follow the same transport process.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Create a shared transport reference</h3><p>Link the load, parties, equipment, quotation and accepted plan to a D-ID.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Prepare the journey</h3><p>Coordinate route constraints, permit requirements, supporting documents and approval status.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Coordinate execution</h3><p>Provide permissioned updates and controlled handovers for dispatchers, drivers and partners.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Preserve evidence</h3><p>Keep a traceable record of relevant decisions, documents, changes and delivery events.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="scenario" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">ILLUSTRATIVE USE CASE</p>
      <h2 id="example-title">Loading time changes after the transport has been arranged.</h2>
      <div class="compare">
        <article><span>COMMON WORKFLOW TODAY</span><p>The change may appear in an email, while the driver, permit documents and dispatcher refer to different versions. The team must reconcile each source.</p></article>
        <article><span>WITH DAJC · INTENDED WORKFLOW</span><p>The transport's D-ID would link an approved change, the affected operational steps and the relevant documents for authorised participants to confirm.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="small">Illustrative scenario, not a measured customer outcome or a promise of time savings. Authority decisions on permits remain with the competent authorities.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="principle" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">OUR DESIGN PRINCIPLE</p>
      <h2 id="approach-title">Connect existing systems. Do not force companies to replace them.</h2>
      <p>Planned interoperability may include APIs, connectors and controlled document exchange where technically and legally available. Specific third-party integrations and permit automation depend on real agreements, access, validation and competent authority approval.</p>
      <a href="/testing">Read about Platform testing 2027 →</a>
    </section>

    <MarketResearchForm product="platform" />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .product-page{position:relative;z-index:2;width:min(1140px,calc(100% - 2.6rem));margin:auto;padding:clamp(3rem,7vw,6rem) 0 6rem;}
  .eyebrow{color:var(--dajc-orange);font:500 .72rem 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;}
  h1,h2,h3{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;color:var(--dajc-white);}
  h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5.5rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.6rem 0 1.5rem;}
  h1 em{color:var(--dajc-orange);font-style:normal;}
  h2{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3.3vw,2.8rem);line-height:1.12;margin:.45rem 0 1.2rem;max-width:25ch;}
  h3{font-size:1.12rem;margin:.1rem 0 .7rem;}
  p{line-height:1.7;color:var(--dajc-muted);}
  .lead{max-width:78ch;font-size:clamp(1.05rem,1.7vw,1.23rem);color:#c5d4e5;}
  .hero{padding:1.6rem 0 clamp(3.5rem,8vw,6rem);}
  .status{max-width:75ch;border-left:3px solid var(--dajc-orange);background:rgba(255,159,0,.08);padding:.9rem 1.15rem;color:#d9e0eb;}
  .actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;margin-top:1.7rem;}
  .button,.outline{display:inline-flex;min-height:48px;align-items:center;padding:0 1.2rem;border-radius:8px;font:700 .8rem 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;text-decoration:none;}
  .button{background:var(--dajc-orange);color:#061A33;}
  .outline{border:1px solid #7087a0;color:#e4eaf2;}
  .small{font-size:.79rem;max-width:80ch;}
  section:not(.hero){border-top:1px solid var(--dajc-line);padding:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4rem) 0;}
  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin-top:2rem;}
  .grid article,.compare article{border:1px solid var(--dajc-line);border-radius:12px;padding:1.4rem;background:rgba(7,33,66,.72);}
  .grid article p{margin:0;}
  .num{font:.75rem 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--dajc-orange);display:block;margin-bottom:.7rem;}
  .section-lead{max-width:80ch;font-size:1.08rem;}
  .steps{display:grid;gap:.8rem;margin-top:2rem;max-width:900px;}
  .steps article{display:flex;gap:1.5rem;align-items:flex-start;border-bottom:1px solid var(--dajc-line);padding:1rem 0;}
  .steps article>span{font:600 1.2rem 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--dajc-orange);}
  .steps article p{margin:0;}
  .compare{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:2rem 0 0;}
  .compare span{font:.7rem 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--dajc-orange);letter-spacing:.08em;}
  .principle a{color:var(--dajc-orange);}
  @media(max-width:700px){.grid,.compare{grid-template-columns:1fr}.product-page{width:min(100% - 2rem,1140px)}}
</style>
